  "notes": "Compton’s virtuoso bassist-producer — the harmonic and bass-line engine of the West Coast jazz-rap axis. **The parameter to model is bass as a LEAD voice**: a six-string tuned BEADGC covering C1 to well above the guitar register, playing fast 16th runs. So the bassline is the busiest and highest-reaching in the whole roster, and the register deliberately overlaps what would elsewhere be melody. Jazz-fusion harmony — m9, maj7#11, 13ths, rapid ii–V movement, chromatic voice-leading and frequent modulation. ⚠ `medium`: instrument, tuning and harmonic lineage are documented; drum and tempo parameters are inferred and marked `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
